    "created_at": "2022-05-31T18:12:13Z",
    "updated_at": "2022-05-31T18:12:13Z",
    "body": "The use of processResponseConsumeBody in script fetching is quite recent and is part of a general slow movement toward updating things to use the new Fetch callbacks. We indeed do not seem to be using it quite correctly.\r\n\r\nFor the more general question, I agree there's not much to be done here besides adding \"be careful\" wording. E.g., `<img>` and stylesheet probably also need access to the raw bytes, at least for some part of the spec. And then they just need to guard any web-developer-exposed access behind the opaqueness.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
